**src/cli.ts**
- In `run`, add a `done` branch before the usage fallback: parse `rest[0]` with `Number`. If `!Number.isInteger(id)`, return `{ out: \`error: not a whole number: ${rest[0]}\`\n`, todos, code: 1 }` (todos unchanged). Otherwise call `markDone(todos, id)` in a try/catch: on `RangeError` return `{ out: \`error: ${e.message}\`\n`, todos, code: 1 } (unchanged); on success `{ out: \`done: ${todo.text}\`\n`, todos: next, code: 0 }` where `todo.text` is the text of the now-done todo. Update the usage line to `usage: todo add <text> | list | done <id>`.
- Note `done` with no args hits `Number(undefined)` = NaN → the error path, so no extra guard needed.

